  fg apps                                   app-launch smoke
  fg homepage                               production-profile build + native boot-smoke + restore normal build
  fg critique                               ADVISORY code-critique view (~5 s, read-only, never gates):
                                            every ratchet's "tighten me now" + stale-allowlist NOTE,
                                            plus the 5 censuses' summary counts (public/private calls,
                                            hierarchy duplication, property placement, ARGUMENT HOLES
                                            -- what `positional-hole` cannot see -- and WIDGET
                                            CONFORMANCE, whose 2 ratcheted facets also gate the build
                                            at a non-zero FLOOR). The
                                            Critic Browser analogue. jscpd/jsinspect stay on-demand.
  fg doc-narration [--full]                 RATCHET: changelog prose in the PRESENT-TENSE doc buckets
                                            (docs/architecture + docs/tooling). Fails when a file's
                                            count RISES — the docs-side twin of the comment-narration
                                            stink. ⛔ specs/ is NOT scanned (a spec's change statements
                                            are load-bearing), nor are plans/ archive/ measurements/,
                                            which are chronological by design. --write-baseline banks
                                            a clean-up; `<!-- narration-ok: why -->` exempts a line.
                                            Also fails on any closed item (`- [x]`) left in
                                            docs/BACKLOG.md, a hard zero (BACKLOG_CLOSED_ITEM).
                                            Also rides the gauntlet's refs leg (not the build: docs
                                            prose must not block a build).
  fg cc [coffee-cc flags|paths]             Cognitive Complexity (SonarSource S3776) of the CoffeeScript
                                            source (npm pkg coffeescript-cognitive-complexity). Read-only,
                                            no build/browser. `fg cc` = top methods over src; also
                                            --by-class | --by-file | --explain <file> | --top=N | --json.
  fg pinsweep                               EVERY ADVERTISED PIN MUST RESOLVE (~5s): a PinSpec names
                                            its setter by STRING, so an unresolved one accepts a wire
                                            and silently does nothing. Also checks every `announces`.
  fg graph                                  WIDGET-GRAPH LIVENESS CONTRACT (~35s, gauntlet wave-A
                                            leg): the storage leg gates the classifier's IDEMPOTENCE,
                                            this gates its SEMANTICS via the real drain — wire death
                                            severs, wire-into-bin-resident shelves (and relays via
                                            the fixpoint), command edges confer nothing, close asks
                                            anyReferenceOrWireIntoWdgt, mixin super chains terminate.
  fg menusweep                              CLICK EVERY MENU ITEM (~6s): fires every reachable menu
                                            action and fails on a throw — the RUNTIME half of menu
                                            wiring, whose static half runs on the build
                                            (check-menu-actions.js). Catches what no text scan can:
                                            a parameter that IS read and is read as the WRONG THING
                                            (slot 1 of ButtonWdgt's dispatch is the MENU ITEM).
                                            Also a gauntlet wave-A leg.
  fg lazyprobe                              the index.html laziness invariants — every app icon drawn
                                            with NO app class, the Examples folder empty until opened,
                                            one click fetching one app. THE ONLY THING THAT CAN SEE
                                            THIS: the suite runs eager-everything on a page with no
                                            desktop. Also runs in the gauntlet's parts leg (sampled).
  fg hypopart <paths...>                    "what if these files were a part?" — inheritance edges,
                                            unguarded references and cross-part callers, using the
                                            BUILD GATE'S own classifier (never a grep)
  fg whatpins [--profile p] [--list]        why is each class in the boot image? Walks from src/boot
                                            and reports (1) what no boot path reaches — movable today,
                                            transitively — and (2) SOLE ROUTES: one class holding a
                                            whole subtree in the image. Section 2 is questions, not
                                            findings. `--why <Class>`. (Its self-test runs on every build.)
  fg fingerprint [profile] [baseref]        MEASURE a packaging change: build <profile> at <baseref>
                                            in a throwaway sibling worktree, build it from the working
                                            tree, diff the fingerprints. Defaults: homepage HEAD.
                                            Leaves the build tree on <profile> — 'fg build' restores.
  fg lint                                   pre-build static checks (~2 s): node --check every git-CHANGED
                                            test .js + the coffee syntax gate if any .coffee changed.
                                            gauntlet/presuite run it first automatically.
  fg status                                 one-shot re-orientation: repos, build freshness, tests,
                                            zombie browsers, fg verdicts (read-only, <2s)
  fg killz                                  kill leftover headless test browsers
build/suite/gauntlet/homepage also maintain /tmp/fg-<cmd>.verdict: "RUNNING since …" while
running, "<CMD> EXIT=<rc> …" when done — cat it to check a backgrounded run (never poll-loop).
EOF
}

cmd="${1:-help}"; shift 2>/dev/null || true
case "$cmd" in
  build)
    verdict_start build
    if fg_build "$@"; then ban "BUILD OK"; verdict_end build 0 "OK"
    else verdict_end build 1 "FAILED"; exit 1; fi ;;
  suite)
    verdict_start suite
    if fg_suite "$@"; then ban "SUITE OK"; verdict_end suite 0 "OK"
    else ban "SUITE FAILED"; verdict_end suite 1 "FAILED"; exit 1; fi ;;
  census)
    # The ARRANGE-IDEMPOTENCE ORACLE (assessment §6.1 rule-2 corollary / §6.4): boots the built
    # world, opens the app battery + basement + window-hosts, resizes everything, then post-order
    # force-re-lays EVERY widget at its current frame — ANY mover fails (as do battery skips and
    # page errors). Run it for any arrange/engine change. ~10s: ONE page, the whole battery +
    # sweep runs synchronously in one page.evaluate — no macro cadence, no pixels (measured
    # 2026-07-17; the old ~90-120s note predated the single-evaluate form). Needs a FRESH build.
    verdict_start census
    kill_browsers
    if ( cd "$FT" && to 300 node scripts/staleness-census.js "$@" ); then
      ban "CENSUS OK"; verdict_end census 0 "OK"
    else ban "CENSUS FAILED"; verdict_end census 1 "FAILED"; exit 1; fi ;;
  revisits)
    # The SETTLE-RE-VISIT standing gate (sizing-model unification U4, plan §9.8): full suite
    # under the re-visit audit prelude, then assert the (test → flush class-multiset) profile
    # equals scripts/revisit-baseline.json. New signature = convergence regression; vanished =
    # improvement to bake in consciously (node scripts/revisit-gate.js --write-baseline).
    # ~2 min. Needs a FRESH build.
    verdict_start revisits
    kill_browsers
    ( cd "$FT" && to 600 node scripts/revisit-gate.js "$@" ); vrc=$?
    if [ $vrc -eq 0 ]; then ban "REVISITS OK"; verdict_end revisits 0 "OK"
    elif [ $vrc -eq 3 ]; then ban "REVISITS INFRA-FLAKE (a shard dropped twice — re-run; not a result)"; verdict_end revisits 3 "INFRA-FLAKE"; exit 3
    else ban "REVISITS FAILED"; verdict_end revisits 1 "FAILED"; exit 1; fi ;;
  storage)
    # The bin/shelf storage DEEP AUDIT (Tier B, bin-shelf-eager-sorting-plan.md Phase 5): full
    # suite under the storage prelude — at each test's end (resetWorld entry) force-drain the
    # pending sort, reclassify FROM SCRATCH and assert ZERO proposed moves (idempotence — the
    # check the always-on Tier A token guard structurally cannot do) + structural residue.
    # The profile must be EMPTY; no baseline file on purpose. ~2 min. Needs a FRESH build.
    verdict_start storage
    kill_browsers
    ( cd "$FT" && to 900 node scripts/storage-invariant-gate.js "$@" ); vrc=$?
    if [ $vrc -eq 0 ]; then ban "STORAGE OK"; verdict_end storage 0 "OK"
    elif [ $vrc -eq 3 ]; then ban "STORAGE INFRA-FLAKE (a shard dropped twice — re-run; not a result)"; verdict_end storage 3 "INFRA-FLAKE"; exit 3
    else ban "STORAGE FAILED"; verdict_end storage 1 "FAILED"; exit 1; fi ;;
  vmtruth)
    # The VM-truth object-lifetime gate (Arc B): full suite under the forced-GC prelude —
    # collectibility oracle + post-GC heap-floor ceiling + INVALID-on-unmeasured. ~2 min.
    # Needs a FRESH build. Chrome-only by design.
    verdict_start vmtruth
    kill_browsers
    ( cd "$FT" && to 900 node scripts/vm-truth-gate.js "$@" ); vrc=$?
    if [ $vrc -eq 0 ]; then ban "VMTRUTH OK"; verdict_end vmtruth 0 "OK"
    elif [ $vrc -eq 2 ]; then ban "VMTRUTH INVALID (not a result — measured nothing)"; verdict_end vmtruth 2 "INVALID"; exit 2
    elif [ $vrc -eq 3 ]; then ban "VMTRUTH INFRA-FLAKE (a shard dropped twice — re-run; not a result)"; verdict_end vmtruth 3 "INFRA-FLAKE"; exit 3
    else ban "VMTRUTH FAILED"; verdict_end vmtruth 1 "FAILED"; exit 1; fi ;;
  test)
    [ $# -ge 1 ] || { usage; exit 2; }
    kill_browsers; ( cd "$FT" && to 240 node scripts/run-macro-test-headless.js "$@" ) ;;
  fuzz)
    # Glyph-atlas delay fault injection. THREE-WAY verdict — the whole point of the tool is that
    # INVALID is not a pass and not a fail: the prototype produced four invalid runs in one morning
    # and three printed `failed: 0`, which reads as a clean pass. So exit 2 gets its OWN loud banner
    # and its own verdict text; it must never be collapsed into OK or FAILED.
    # NOT a gauntlet leg (owner-declined 2026-07-29): nondeterministic by construction.
    verdict_start fuzz
    kill_browsers
    ( cd "$FT" && to 5400 node scripts/run-atlas-fuzz.js "$@" ); rc=$?
    case $rc in
      0) ban "FUZZ OK"; verdict_end fuzz 0 "OK" ;;
      1) ban "FUZZ FAILED — a pixel read is NOT covered by the text-settle gate (do NOT recapture)"
         verdict_end fuzz 1 "FAILED (finding)"; exit 1 ;;
      *) ban "FUZZ INVALID (not a result) — the run measured nothing; do not read it as a pass"
         verdict_end fuzz "$rc" "INVALID (not a result)"; exit "$rc" ;;
    esac ;;
  diffpage)
    # Build a ref|now|CSS-diff review page. Needs a build reflecting the change under review.
    # Read-only wrt references. Serial dumping, one browser at a time. --assemble-only skips dumping.
    # THREE outcomes per test x dpr (CHANGED / UNCHANGED / INVALID, lib/diffwork.js): exit 2 = the page
    # is NOT a complete review (a dump that measured nothing, an undecodable or unpaired image).
    kill_browsers; ( cd "$FT" && node scripts/make-diff-page.js "$@" ); rc=$?
    case $rc in
      0) ;;
      2) ban "DIFFPAGE INCOMPLETE — some group is INVALID (or an image is undecodable/unpaired): do NOT read the page as 'unchanged' there"; exit 2 ;;
      *) exit "$rc" ;;
    esac ;;
  classify)
    # ADVISORY ONLY — read-only over an existing diffpage work dir; no browser, no build, no refs
    # touched. Its BENIGN? verdicts are SUSPECTED (no region manifest yet), so they may never be
    # acted on unread: confirm in fg diffpage, then recapture by hand if the change really is benign.
    ( cd "$FT" && node scripts/classify-diff.js "$@" ) ;;
  cc)
    # Cognitive Complexity (SonarSource S3776) of the CoffeeScript source, via the npm
    # package coffeescript-cognitive-complexity (a Fizzygum devDependency; bin coffee-cc).
    # Read-only — no build, no browser. Defaults the target to Fizzygum/src when no path
    # arg is given (so `fg cc` and `fg cc --by-class` both scan the whole tree); otherwise
    # flags/paths pass straight through: `fg cc --explain src/serialization/Serializer.coffee`.
    [ -x "$FZ/node_modules/.bin/coffee-cc" ] || { echo "fg cc: coffee-cc not installed — run: ( cd \"$FZ\" && npm install )"; exit 3; }
    havepath=0; for a in "$@"; do case "$a" in -*) ;; *) havepath=1 ;; esac; done
    [ $havepath -eq 1 ] || set -- "$@" src
    ( cd "$FZ" && node_modules/.bin/coffee-cc "$@" ) ;;
  recapture)
    # Gated recapture (scripts/recapture.js): recapture the named tests -- or --auto to DISCOVER the
    # stale set from a suite run -- with NO BUILDS AT ALL (the built world serves Fizzygum-tests/tests
    # through a symlink, so a deleted reference is gone at once and a captured one is live at once),
    # then RE-RUN THE FULL SUITE at each dpr and print an unambiguous COMPLETE/INCOMPLETE verdict, so a
    # silently-incomplete recapture is impossible. Prefer this over eyeballing a footprint. ONE pointer
    # kind per run: `--pointer=finger` recaptures the finger references (default mouse), so a full wave
    # is `fg recapture --auto` then `fg recapture --auto --pointer=finger`. Captures run `--jobs=N` at a
    # time (default 6) and are recompressed in one parallel pass; measured 2026-10-16, a full mouse wave
    # projects to ~30 min (was ~7 h serial). (Fast
    # non-gated single-test capture, no completeness check:
    # node scripts/capture-macro-test-references.js <name> --clean --dprs=1,2)
    # Minutes-long, so it writes a verdict like every other long op -- its absence once left a
    # background `until grep RECAPTURE EXIT /tmp/fg-recapture.verdict` waiter spinning forever on a
    # file that was never going to appear (the sibling recapture-inspector had one, this did not).
    [ $# -ge 1 ] || { usage; exit 2; }
    verdict_start recapture
    kill_browsers
    if ( cd "$FT" && node scripts/recapture.js "$@" ); then
      ban "RECAPTURE OK"; verdict_end recapture 0 "OK"
    else ban "RECAPTURE FAILED"; verdict_end recapture 1 "FAILED"; exit 1; fi ;;
  run-sequence)
    # Run a NAMED SUBSET of tests in ONE shared world (scripts/run-sequence-headless.js) -- reproduce a
    # cross-test state leak (DETERMINISM.md §2d): `fg run-sequence <predecessor> <victim>`.
    kill_browsers
    ( cd "$FT" && node scripts/run-sequence-headless.js "$@" ) ;;
  recapture-inspector)
    # The inspector member-list CHURN SET: the tests whose screenshots render a live widget member
    # list, so a benign new member that every Widget carries as an OWN field changes their pixels. (A
    # Widget METHOD or class-body field reaches far fewer: the inspector hides inherited members by
    # default, so it lists one only where the inspected object is a plain Widget.)
    # The set is READ from Fizzygum-tests/scripts/inspector-churn-set.json — the one list, which
    # classify-diff.js also reads, as corroboration — through its one reader, scripts/lib/
    # inspector-churn-set.js, and is re-derived by planting such a field:
    # scripts/derive-inspector-churn-set.js (--check | --write).
    # A name there with no tests/ directory REFUSES the run (exit 2) before anything is recaptured, as
    # recapture.js refuses a name that is not a test.
    # After a benign framework-member change turns them red, this ONE command hands the whole set to
    # the gated recapture (scripts/recapture.js) once per POINTER KIND — mouse, then finger, since these
    # tests carry finger references too and the same change leaves those stale for `fg finger`. Each
    # run recaptures at dpr 1 and 2, re-runs the full suite of its kind and prints COMPLETE/INCOMPLETE;
    # a mouse-only test is passed over in the finger run as TEST SKIPPED. No builds (the world serves
    # tests/ through the js/tests link), long enough to background. Deterministic capture ⇒ if the
    # member list did NOT change, the recapture is byte-identical and git status stays clean. Close
    # with a normal fg gauntlet before committing.
    verdict_start recapture-inspector
    t_all=$SECONDS; failed=""
    # stdout = the names, one per line; the stale entries, or a malformed-file error, go to stderr,
    # straight to the terminal. A tests/ tree that is not all tests (TESTS_DIRECTORY_MALFORMED) is
    # its own refusal (exit 3): the churn set is not what is wrong then.
    churn=$( cd "$FT" && node -e '
      let s;
      try { s = require("./scripts/lib/inspector-churn-set").loadInspectorChurnSet(); }
      catch (e) { process.stderr.write("  " + e.message + "\n"); process.exit(/^TESTS_DIRECTORY_MALFORMED/.test(e.message) ? 3 : 2); }
      if (s.missing.length) { process.stderr.write("  not a test:\n" + s.missing.map(t => "    " + t + "\n").join("")); process.exit(2); }
      process.stdout.write(s.tests.join("\n") + "\n");' ) || {
      if [ $? -eq 3 ]; then
        ban "RECAPTURE-INSPECTOR REFUSED — Fizzygum-tests/tests/ holds a directory that is no test (above); nothing recaptured."
        verdict_end recapture-inspector 2 "REFUSED — tests/ malformed"; exit 2
      fi
      ban "RECAPTURE-INSPECTOR REFUSED — Fizzygum-tests/scripts/inspector-churn-set.json is not a current list of tests (above); nothing recaptured. Re-derive it: node scripts/derive-inspector-churn-set.js --write"
      verdict_end recapture-inspector 2 "REFUSED — churn set not current"; exit 2; }
    n_churn=$(printf '%s\n' "$churn" | grep -c .)
    echo "  recapturing the $n_churn tests of the inspector churn set (Fizzygum-tests/scripts/inspector-churn-set.json)"
    for kind in mouse finger; do
      kill_browsers
      pointer_flag=""; [ "$kind" = finger ] && pointer_flag="--pointer=finger"
      lg="/tmp/fg-recapture-inspector-$kind.log"
      echo "  $kind references: node scripts/recapture.js --dprs=1,2 $pointer_flag <the $n_churn tests>   (log: $lg)"
      # shellcheck disable=SC2086  # $churn is the name list, one word per test
      if ( cd "$FT" && node scripts/recapture.js --dprs=1,2 $pointer_flag $churn ) >"$lg" 2>&1
      then echo "  ✓ $kind: RECAPTURE COMPLETE"
      else rc=$?; echo "  ✗ $kind: recapture.js exit $rc"; failed="$failed $kind(exit $rc)"
      fi
      grep -E 'VERDICT:' "$lg" | sed 's/^ */    /'
    done
    if [ -n "$failed" ]; then ban "RECAPTURE-INSPECTOR FAILED —$failed (logs: /tmp/fg-recapture-inspector-<kind>.log)"; verdict_end recapture-inspector 1 "FAILED —$failed"; exit 1; fi
    ban "RECAPTURE-INSPECTOR OK — $n_churn tests, mouse + finger, recaptured and gated in $(( (SECONDS-t_all)/60 ))m; close with fg gauntlet before committing"
    verdict_end recapture-inspector 0 "OK $n_churn tests mouse+finger total=$((SECONDS-t_all))s" ;;
  apps)
    kill_browsers; ( cd "$FT" && to 300 node scripts/smoke-apps-headless.js "$@" ) ;;
  presuite)
    # INNER-LOOP tier (plan P1.5): build + [dpr1 suite (8 shards) ∥ sharded paint audit ∥ fracplane dpr2 rider].
    # Iterate with presuite; close a phase/commit point with the full gauntlet.
    verdict_start presuite
    suite_profile_or_refuse "$@" || { verdict_end presuite 2 "REFUSED — the profile ships no harness page"; exit 2; }
    PRESUITE_LEGS=$(legs names presuite) && INFRA_LEGS=$(legs names infra) && leg_list_ok "$PRESUITE_LEGS" \
      || { legs names presuite; verdict_end presuite 2 "REFUSED — the leg table (buildSystem/legs.js) cannot be run"; exit 2; }
    legs_pending presuite $PRESUITE_LEGS
    t_all=$SECONDS
    run_lint || { verdict_end presuite 1 "FAILED — lint"; exit 1; }
    fg_build "$@" || { verdict_end presuite 1 "FAILED — build"; exit 1; }
    kill_browsers
    WAVE_RES=""; tally=""; ok=1; warn=0
    FG_SUITE_SHARDS=8
    ban "PRESUITE WAVE: $(legs banner presuite)   — the suite at 8 shards, paint at 5"
    run_wave $PRESUITE_LEGS
    collect_and_retry
    legs_all_ran $PRESUITE_LEGS
    total_secs=$((SECONDS-t_all))
    if [ $ok -eq 1 ]; then ban "PRESUITE OK —$tally — total $((total_secs/60))m$((total_secs%60))s"; verdict_end presuite 0 "OK —$tally total=${total_secs}s"
    else ban "PRESUITE FAILED —$tally — total $((total_secs/60))m$((total_secs%60))s"; verdict_end presuite 1 "FAILED —$tally total=${total_secs}s"; exit 1; fi ;;
  gauntlet)
    verdict_start gauntlet
    suite_profile_or_refuse "$@" || { verdict_end gauntlet 2 "REFUSED — the profile ships no harness page"; exit 2; }
    # the legs, from the one table (buildSystem/legs.js); a table fg cannot run refuses the run, never runs a wave of nothing
    GAUNTLET_LEGS=$(legs names gauntlet) && INFRA_LEGS=$(legs names infra) && WAVE_A=$(legs names A) && WAVE_B=$(legs names B) \
      && WAVE_C=$(legs names C) && WAVE_D=$(legs names D) && leg_list_ok "$GAUNTLET_LEGS" && leg_list_ok "$WAVE_A" \
      && leg_list_ok "$WAVE_B" && leg_list_ok "$WAVE_C" && leg_list_ok "$WAVE_D" \
      || { legs names gauntlet; verdict_end gauntlet 2 "REFUSED — the leg table (buildSystem/legs.js) cannot be run"; exit 2; }
    # every leg run_wave launches must be listed here, or its log keeps the PREVIOUS run's
    # contents for the whole lint+build minute and reads as this run's result (`storage` was
    # missing and did exactly that — showing a stale rc=0 while this run had not started it).
    legs_pending gauntlet $GAUNTLET_LEGS
    if [ "${FG_GAUNTLET_SERIAL:-0}" = 1 ]; then
      # ---------- SERIAL escape hatch: the table's legs one after another, in wave order — the same rows the waves run,
      # so it cannot run fewer; the suites at their standalone 8 shards, as the serial retry runs them ----------
      fg_build "$@" || { verdict_end gauntlet 1 "FAILED — build"; exit 1; }
      tally=""; ok=1
      FG_SUITE_SHARDS=8
      for n in $GAUNTLET_LEGS; do
        kill_browsers; run_leg "$n"; rc=$?
        echo "--- $n ---"; leg_headline "$n"
        if [ $rc -eq 0 ]; then tally="$tally $n:PASS"
        elif [ $rc -eq 3 ] && infra_leg "$n"; then tally="$tally $n:INFRA-FLAKE"; echo "⚠ $n: INFRA shard-drop (exit 3) — zero failed tests, not a failure (plan P6)"
        else tally="$tally $n:FAIL"; ok=0; tail -15 "/tmp/fg-$n.log"; fi
      done
      if [ $ok -eq 1 ]; then ban "GAUNTLET OK —$tally"; verdict_end gauntlet 0 "OK —$tally"
      else ban "GAUNTLET FAILED —$tally"; verdict_end gauntlet 1 "FAILED —$tally"; exit 1; fi
    else
      # ---------- PARALLEL path (plan P1: two waves + failed-leg serial retry) ----------
      t_all=$SECONDS
      run_lint || { verdict_end gauntlet 1 "FAILED — lint"; exit 1; }
      fg_build "$@" || { verdict_end gauntlet 1 "FAILED — build"; exit 1; }
      kill_browsers   # ONCE, up front; the waves run with the cull suppressed
      WAVE_RES=""; tally=""; ok=1; warn=0
      # the waves are the table's (buildSystem/legs.js says why each leg sits in its wave); the shard counts are fg's
      ban "WAVE A: ${WAVE_A// / ∥ }"
      run_wave $WAVE_A
      FG_GATE_SHARDS=4
      ban "WAVE B: ${WAVE_B// / ∥ }   (gates at $FG_GATE_SHARDS shards)"
      run_wave $WAVE_B
      FG_GATE_SHARDS=6
      ban "WAVE C: ${WAVE_C// / ∥ }   (gates at $FG_GATE_SHARDS shards)"
      run_wave $WAVE_C
      ban "WAVE D: ${WAVE_D// / ∥ }"
      run_wave $WAVE_D
      # serial retries (if any) run each failed leg alone at its standalone shape
      FG_SUITE_SHARDS=8; FG_GATE_SHARDS=6
      collect_and_retry
      legs_all_ran $GAUNTLET_LEGS
      total_secs=$((SECONDS-t_all))
      if [ $ok -eq 1 ]; then
        if [ $warn -eq 1 ]; then ban "GAUNTLET OK (load-flake warning, see above) —$tally — total $((total_secs/60))m$((total_secs%60))s"; verdict_end gauntlet 0 "OK(warn) —$tally total=${total_secs}s"
        else ban "GAUNTLET OK —$tally — total $((total_secs/60))m$((total_secs%60))s"; verdict_end gauntlet 0 "OK —$tally total=${total_secs}s"; fi
      else ban "GAUNTLET FAILED —$tally — total $((total_secs/60))m$((total_secs%60))s"; verdict_end gauntlet 1 "FAILED —$tally total=${total_secs}s"; exit 1; fi
    fi ;;
  homepage)
    verdict_start homepage
    fg_build --profile homepage || { verdict_end homepage 1 "FAILED — homepage build"; exit 1; }
    kill_browsers; ( cd "$FT" && to 300 node scripts/smoke-boot-headless.js --production ); hrc=$?
    ban "restoring normal build…"; fg_build || { verdict_end homepage 1 "FAILED — restoring normal build"; exit 1; }
    if [ $hrc -eq 0 ]; then ban "HOMEPAGE BOOT OK (normal build restored)"; verdict_end homepage 0 "OK"
    else ban "HOMEPAGE SMOKE FAILED (normal build restored)"; verdict_end homepage 1 "FAILED — smoke"; exit 1; fi ;;
  menusweep)
    kill_browsers
    ( cd "$FT" && node scripts/menu-click-sweep-headless.js "$@" ); rc=$?
    [ $rc -eq 0 ] && ban "MENU CLICK SWEEP OK" || ban "MENU CLICK SWEEP FAILED"
    exit $rc ;;
  finger)
    verdict_start finger
    if fg_suite --pointer=finger --browser=webkit --dpr=2 "$@"; then ban "FINGER SUITE OK"; verdict_end finger 0 "OK"
    else ban "FINGER SUITE FAILED"; verdict_end finger 1 "FAILED"; exit 1; fi ;;
  pinsweep)
    kill_browsers
    ( cd "$FT" && node scripts/pin-sweep-headless.js "$@" ); rc=$?
    [ $rc -eq 0 ] && ban "PIN SWEEP OK" || ban "PIN SWEEP FAILED"
    exit $rc ;;
  graph)
    kill_browsers
    ( cd "$FT" && node scripts/graph-liveness-headless.js "$@" ); rc=$?
    [ $rc -eq 0 ] && ban "GRAPH LIVENESS OK" || ban "GRAPH LIVENESS FAILED"
    exit $rc ;;
  lazyprobe)
    # THE ONLY THING THAT CAN SEE LAZINESS. createDesktop runs only `if world.isIndexPage`, and the
    # harness page + index-sw.html preset FIZZYGUM_EAGER_ALL_PARTS, so the SystemTest suite runs on a
    # world where the desktop does not exist and nothing is lazy: a green gauntlet is NOT evidence
    # that an on-demand path works. It shipped four broken doors, a five-of-six palette and a
    # two-content-lists toolbar in one day before this existed.
    # The same script runs as part of the gauntlet's `parts` leg, where it SAMPLES three icons for
    # the per-click isolation check; here it does all of them.
    ( cd "$FT" && node scripts/parts-lazy-icons-headless.js --exhaustive ) ;;

  hypopart)
    # "What if these files were a part?" -- answered with the build gate's OWN classifier
    # (buildSystem/lib/part-edge-scan.js), never a grep: it strips comments and string literals,
    # and prose naming a class has produced false hits in two separate arcs.
    [ $# -gt 0 ] || { echo "usage: fg hypopart <file-or-dir>...   (paths relative to Fizzygum/)"; exit 2; }
    ( cd "$FZ" && node buildSystem/hypothetical-part.js "$@" ) ;;

  whatpins)
    # The companion question to hypopart's. hypopart asks "would THIS grouping work"; this asks
    # "what should I be grouping at all" -- by walking the boot path instead of asking who names
    # whom, which is the hop pinned-by-lazy-parts.js cannot make (it reads one level, over the
    # partition as it stands, so a lazy class two hops behind an eager one reads back "must not
    # move" -- which is how 9.5 KB of C-F icon art stayed in production until it was spotted by eye).
    # NOT a gate: section 2 ranks design questions, and most of its answers are "no, that is core".
    ( cd "$FZ" && node buildSystem/what-pins-core.js "$@" ) ;;

  fingerprint)
    # MEASURE a packaging change instead of estimating it: build <profile> at a BASELINE ref in a
    # throwaway sibling worktree, build it again from the working tree, and diff the fingerprints.
    #
    # WARN THE TRAP THIS EXISTS TO REMOVE. Fizzygum-tests must be a real WORKTREE, never a symlink:
    # generate-pre-compiled-headless.js and build-tree-fingerprint.js both resolve their paths from
    # __dirname, so through a symlink they address the REAL build tree while the build addresses the
    # baseline one. Doing that by hand once produced a void measurement AND silently overwrote
    # Fizzygum-builds/latest -- with no error at all. Only node_modules is symlinked.
    prof="${1:-homepage}"; base="${2:-HEAD}"
    BASEDIR="$ROOT/../Fizzygum-fingerprint-baseline"
    verdict_start fingerprint
    rm -rf "$BASEDIR"
    git -C "$FZ" worktree prune; git -C "$FT" worktree prune
    mkdir -p "$BASEDIR/Fizzygum-builds"
    git -C "$FZ" worktree add --detach "$BASEDIR/Fizzygum" "$base" >/dev/null 2>&1 \
      || { echo "fg fingerprint: cannot create a worktree of Fizzygum at '$base'"; verdict_end fingerprint 1 "FAILED — worktree"; exit 1; }
    git -C "$FT" worktree add --detach "$BASEDIR/Fizzygum-tests" HEAD >/dev/null 2>&1 \
      || { echo "fg fingerprint: cannot create a worktree of Fizzygum-tests"; verdict_end fingerprint 1 "FAILED — worktree"; exit 1; }
    ln -sfn "$FT/node_modules" "$BASEDIR/Fizzygum-tests/node_modules"
    # font-assets/ is gitignored, so a worktree has none, and every profile that ships an SWCanvas page copies it:
    # without this the candidate shows its ~4,500 files as extra whatever the change. The build copies through the
    # link (`cp -R font-assets/*`), so the baseline tree gets real files.
    [ -d "$FZ/font-assets" ] && ln -sfn "$FZ/font-assets" "$BASEDIR/Fizzygum/font-assets"
    # A baseline from before fg was versioned (Fizzygum/fg) looks for it in the umbrella, as fg then lived there:
    # give it this one, or its build's first gate fails before anything is compared.
    [ -e "$BASEDIR/Fizzygum/fg" ] || cp "$FZ/fg" "$BASEDIR/fg"

    OUT="$FT/.scratch/fingerprints"; mkdir -p "$OUT"
    ban "fingerprint: building '$prof' at BASELINE $base"
    ( cd "$BASEDIR/Fizzygum" && ./build_it_please.sh --profile "$prof" ) >/tmp/fg-fingerprint-base.log 2>&1 \
      || { echo "fg fingerprint: baseline build FAILED — see /tmp/fg-fingerprint-base.log"; verdict_end fingerprint 1 "FAILED — baseline build"; exit 1; }
    ( cd "$BASEDIR/Fizzygum-tests" && node scripts/build-tree-fingerprint.js write "$OUT/base-$prof.txt" ) || exit 1

    ban "fingerprint: building '$prof' from the WORKING TREE"
    ( cd "$FZ" && ./build_it_please.sh --profile "$prof" ) >/tmp/fg-fingerprint-cand.log 2>&1 \
      || { echo "fg fingerprint: candidate build FAILED — see /tmp/fg-fingerprint-cand.log"; verdict_end fingerprint 1 "FAILED — candidate build"; exit 1; }
    ( cd "$FT" && node scripts/build-tree-fingerprint.js write "$OUT/cand-$prof.txt" ) || exit 1

    ban "fingerprint: $prof — BASELINE ($base) vs WORKING TREE"
    ( cd "$FT" && node scripts/build-tree-fingerprint.js compare "$OUT/base-$prof.txt" "$OUT/cand-$prof.txt" ); drc=$?
    git -C "$FZ" worktree remove --force "$BASEDIR/Fizzygum" >/dev/null 2>&1
    git -C "$FT" worktree remove --force "$BASEDIR/Fizzygum-tests" >/dev/null 2>&1
    rm -rf "$BASEDIR"
    ban "fingerprint: the build tree now holds '$prof' — run 'fg build' to restore the dev tree"
    # A DIFFERENCE IS THE POINT here, so a non-zero compare is not a failure: the verdict records
    # that the measurement RAN. Read the diff.
    verdict_end fingerprint 0 "OK — compared $prof (differences: $([ $drc -eq 0 ] && echo none || echo yes))" ;;

  lint)
    run_lint || exit 1 ;;
  stinks)
    # The check-stinks ratchet, callable directly (its comment-* rules are the comments-side twin
    # of doc-narration). `fg stinks` = the full ratchet report the build runs; `fg stinks --list
    # <id>` enumerates one stink's sites (a sweep enumerator, e.g. --list comment-past-receipt).
    # Instant + read-only, so no verdict file.
    ( cd "$FZ" && node buildSystem/check-stinks.js "$@" ) || exit 1 ;;
  doc-narration)
    # The docs-side twin of the `comment-narration` stink. RATCHET over the PRESENT-TENSE doc
    # buckets only (architecture/ + tooling/): specs/ is excluded by owner direction (a spec's
    # change statements are load-bearing), and plans/ archive/ measurements/ are chronological
    # by design. Fails when a file's narration count RISES, and on any closed item left in
    # docs/BACKLOG.md (a hard zero). --full lists every line; --write-baseline banks an
    # improvement. Exit 2 = INVALID (it read nothing), kept as 2. Instant + read-only, so no
    # verdict file.
    ( cd "$FZ" && node buildSystem/check-doc-narration.js "$@" ) || exit $? ;;
  status)
    # One-shot session/post-compaction re-orientation (dev-workflow plan P5). READ-ONLY.
    echo "fg status — $(date '+%F %T')"
    for r in Fizzygum Fizzygum-tests Fizzygum-builds; do
      d="$ROOT/$r"
      b=$(git -C "$d" rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD 2>/dev/null || echo '?')
      sha=$(git -C "$d" rev-parse --short HEAD 2>/dev/null || echo '?')
      dirty=$(git -C "$d" status --porcelain 2>/dev/null | grep -c .)
      ab=$(git -C "$d" rev-list --left-right --count "origin/$b...HEAD" 2>/dev/null | awk '{print "behind="$1" ahead="$2}')
      printf '  %-16s %s @ %s  dirty=%s  %s\n' "$r" "$b" "$sha" "$dirty" "${ab:-(no origin tracking)}"
    done
    BUILT="$ROOT/Fizzygum-builds/latest/index.html"
    if [ ! -f "$BUILT" ]; then echo "  build: MISSING (no $BUILT)"
    else
      # the sources the build compiles: src and the harness (Fizzygum/buildSystem/lib/source-files.js)
      newer=$(find "$FZ/src" "$ROOT/Fizzygum-tests/Automator-and-test-harness-src" -name '*.coffee' -newer "$BUILT" 2>/dev/null | head -3)
      if [ -n "$newer" ]; then echo "  build: STALE — newer source, e.g.:"; echo "$newer" | sed 's/^/           /'
      else echo "  build: FRESH (built $(date -r "$BUILT" '+%F %T'))"; fi
    fi
    echo "  tests: $(ls "$FT/tests" 2>/dev/null | grep -c '^SystemTest_') SystemTests"
    echo "  zombie test browsers: $(pgrep -f 'Chrome for Testing|chrome-headless|puppeteer|webkit' 2>/dev/null | grep -c .)   (fg killz clears)"
    echo "  fg verdicts:"
    found=0
    for v in /tmp/fg-*.verdict; do [ -f "$v" ] || continue; found=1; printf '    %-24s %s\n' "$(basename "$v" .verdict)" "$(cat "$v")"; done
    if [ $found -eq 0 ]; then echo "    (none)"; fi
    ;;
  critique)
    # The Critic Browser analogue (lint-generic-rules-carryover-plan Phase 5): ONE read-only view of
    # the whole ADVISORY tier + every "you could tighten a ratchet now" signal. Nothing here gates and
    # nothing here writes; the gates themselves run on the build. Deliberately EXCLUDES jscpd/jsinspect
    # (minutes-slow — they stay on-demand via Fizzygum/find_duplicated_code.sh / find_similar_code.sh).
    echo "fg critique — $(date '+%F %T')   [ADVISORY — nothing here gates]"
    t0=$(date +%s)
    step(){ # step <label> <cmd…> : run it, print the lines worth seeing, time it
      local label="$1"; shift
      local s=$(date +%s) out
      out=$( cd "$FZ" && "$@" 2>&1 )
      printf '\n── %s (%ss)\n' "$label" "$(( $(date +%s) - s ))"
      echo "$out" | grep -vE '^\s*$' | sed 's/^/   /'
    }
    # 1-5: the ratchets — reprint only the "tighten me" / stale-entry NOTEs and the summaries
    step "stinks — tighten?" bash -c "node ./buildSystem/check-stinks.js | grep -E 'UNDER|NOTE|OK --' || true"
    step "dead-methods — stale allowlist?" bash -c "node ./buildSystem/check-dead-methods.js | grep -E 'NOTE|OK —' || true"
    step "unresolved-sends — stale allowlist?" bash -c "node ./buildSystem/check-unresolved-sends.js | grep -E 'NOTE|OK —' || true"
    step "call-separation — tighten?" bash -c "node ./buildSystem/check-call-separation.js | grep -E 'NOTE|OK —' || true"
    step "complexity ratchets — tighten?" bash -c "node ./buildSystem/check-complexity-ratchets.js | grep -E 'UNDER|NOTE|OK' || true"
    # 6-8: the advisory censuses — summary counts only ( --full for the lists )
    step "census: public/private self-calls" bash -c "node ./buildSystem/census-public-private-calls.js | grep -E '^(stats|by callee class|hard sites|total|narrowed)' || true"
    step "census: hierarchy duplication" bash -c "node ./buildSystem/census-hierarchy-duplication.js | grep -E '^(scanned|IDENTICAL)' || true"
    step "census: property placement" bash -c "node ./buildSystem/census-property-placement.js | grep -E '^(scanned|PULL-UP:)|withheld' || true"
    # widget-practices conformance: the ADVISORY view. Its two ratcheted facets also run as
    # `--gate` on the build; the other four are heuristics that must never gate. Both baselines
    # are FLOORS, so a green ratchet is not an empty inventory.
    step "census: widget conformance" bash -c "node ./buildSystem/census-widget-conformance.js | grep -E '^(\[widget-conformance\]|RATCHETED|ADVISORY|  [0-9]\.)' || true"
    # 9: call arguments — the GATE's own verdict line (holes, extra arguments, positionals into options;
    # every call in both repos, exact zero; it also runs on every build). `--values` on it lists the
    # absences it judges values; the call-site queries are census-call-arity.js's (`<Class…>`, --super=, --call=).
    step "call arguments (the gate's verdict)" bash -c "node ./buildSystem/check-call-arguments.js | grep -E '^\[call-arguments\]' || true"
    printf '\n── total %ss\n' "$(( $(date +%s) - t0 ))"
    echo "advisory only — nothing here gates; see Fizzygum/docs/archive/lint-generic-rules-carryover-plan.md"
    echo "  lists: add --full to any census; machine-readable: --json <file>"
    ;;
  killz)
    kill_browsers; echo "killed leftover headless test browsers (Chrome for Testing / chrome-headless / puppeteer / webkit)" ;;
  *) usage ;;
esac
